-- The runtime half of a structural field constraint: `PropertyWitness`, and a body that reads and
-- writes a field of a type it cannot see.
--
-- Compiled with specialization declined (see the `.generic` marker beside it), so the IR below is
-- the erased form. Property.yana is the same feature specialized, and the two have to agree about
-- what the program means - which is what the run comparison every other fixture does asserts.
--
-- What a witness is: two descriptors and two accessors, interned per owner and field. What a body
-- does with it: load the witness from the environment slot its schema numbered, load the operation
-- from the witness, call it. No name is hashed and nothing is searched, at either end.

data Person {name: Int, age: Int}
data Item {name: Int, cost: Int}

-- One constraint, read only. The result comes back through storage this frame provided, because the
-- field's type is a variable here and there is no register class to hand it back in.
fn (a.name: Int) nameOf(p: a) -> Int = p.name

-- Writing one. `set` consumes what it is handed and releases what the field held, so the caller
-- relocates the replacement into staging storage rather than lending it - which for an Int is a
-- store, and for a type that owed something would be the one relocation it is allowed.
fn (a.name: Int) rename(&p: a, to: Int): p.name = to

-- Two constraints on one variable, at different indices in each record. Nothing in the body depends
-- on where either field is: both are witnesses, and which one each caller passed is the whole of the
-- difference between the two records below.
fn (a.name: Int, a.tag: Int) labelled(p: a) -> Int = nameOf(p) * 100 + p.tag

data Left {name: Int, tag: Int}
data Right {tag: Int, name: Int}

fn main() -> Int:
    let people = nameOf(Person {name: 5, age: 90})
    let items = nameOf(Item {name: 2, cost: 7})

    let &subject = Person {name: 1, age: 2}
    rename(subject, 8)

    -- 100 + 3 = 103, and 600 + 4 = 604.
    let left = labelled(Left {name: 1, tag: 3})
    let right = labelled(Right {tag: 4, name: 6})

    -- 5000 + 200 + 80 + 103 + 604 = 5987
    return people * 1000 + items * 100 + nameOf(subject) * 10 + left + right
